The legal texts come from the Journal officiel de la République du Mali, published by the Secrétariat général du
Gouvernement:

  Journal officiel de la République du Mali, https://sgg-mali.ml/fr/journal-officiel/le-journal-officiel.html
  (issues retrieved 2026-10-28): spécial n°13 of 22 July 2023, n°20 of 4 August 2023, spécial n°21 of
  13 December 2024, n°26 of 28 June 2013 and n°53 of 29 December 2017; and the "Codes en vigueur" copy
  https://sgg-mali.ml/codes/codepenal.pdf.

Attribution: "Texte officiel : Journal officiel de la République du Mali, Secrétariat général du Gouvernement
(sgg-mali.ml)."

sgg-mali.ml states no licence, and whether Malian copyright law excludes official legislative texts from protection
has not been verified. This repository is therefore private; whether and how it may be published is the owner's
decision.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text layer of each issue was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph
per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; structural headings and the Code pénal's bracketed source notes
were gathered into one plan file per act; signatures, promulgation formulas and the Code pénal's annexed table of
contents were left out; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws that made each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. The Government of Mali does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
